    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented the change by adding an email-uniqueness check to `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness check:\n\n- After the telephone conflict check, the controller now calls a new `emailAlreadyUsed(...)` helper and returns `409 CONFLICT` when it matches.\n- `emailAlreadyUsed` compares the candidate's already-normalised (lower-cased) email against every existing owner's email, case-insensitively. A `null`/blank email is never treated as a duplicate, so owners without an email (the common case in the other tests) are unaffected.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test passes and the build succeeds.",
